As you can see, there are a lot of different templates in SOPHIST.

You shall now determine whether a given requirement adheres to the SOPHIST templates and verify their correctness.

Your task is to perform validation of a given requirement. A requirement is valid, if it follows one of the SOPHIST templates.
Be very careful with your decision, as we do not want to have invalid requirements falsely labeled as valid. If you are unsure, label the requirement as invalid and provide a short explanation why it does not fit any of the SOPHIST templates.

In all cases, pay special attention to the following points.
- Mandatory usage of a modal verb (will, shall, should).
- Proper usage of the important placeholders <system> and <object>

Please analyze the given requirement and return your expert validation result.

Answer in the following format:

{
    "reason": "Short reason for the validation result."
    "valid": true | false,
}

Keep the reason short and to the point, for example:

{
    "reason": "Missing correct modal verb."
    "valid": false,
}

If the requirement is valid, the reason shall be null.
{
    "reason": null
    "valid": true,
}
